# Native Scarlet (pnpm desktop:demo) on private Xvfb DISPLAY=:99, 1920x1080.
# Window: Scarlet, cropped to ~960 px in the GIF. Isolated sample interview.
# Save folder: ~/Videos/Exports (cleared first; no replace prompts).
# GTK bookmarks: only file:///home/ubuntu/Videos/Exports. No src-tauri.
# GTK save dialog: Home, Videos, Exports, Other Locations in the sidebar.
# SubRip captions / WebVTT captions filter. Name field on the project name.

$ Xvfb :99 -screen 0 1920x1080x24 -nolisten tcp
# running (tmux)

$ DISPLAY=:99 xfwm4 --compositor=off
# running on :99 only (the session on :1 was left alone)

$ pnpm desktop:demo
# running (tmux scarlet-demo), Vite http://127.0.0.1:5174, binary apps/desktop/src-tauri/target/debug/scarlet-desktop
# launched from /home/ubuntu/Videos/Exports so the GTK dialog cwd is not src-tauri

# Export → Captions (.srt) → Save "~/Videos/Exports/Weekly interview — AI agents.srt"
# Export → Captions (.vtt) → Save "~/Videos/Exports/Weekly interview — AI agents.vtt"
# Range → Custom range, From 0:01.000, To 0:06.000 → Save "~/Videos/Exports/Weekly interview — range.srt"
# Tech brief — GPU shortage → Captions (.srt): Export stays off.

$ cat "/home/ubuntu/Videos/Exports/Weekly interview — AI agents.srt"
1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,400
Welcome back

